# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Deprecation Calendar & Breaking-Change Notice Policy

How this project tells consumers something is going away, and how it tells them
something already changed underneath them. This is a fragment, not a standalone
document role: paste it into whatever plays the `release` role here (see
`RELEASE.md.template` §6, "Deprecating and breaking changes") and fill in the
`<!-- DECIDE -->` markers below it.

These are two related but distinct commitments, kept in one fragment because a
project that answers one without the other usually ends up improvising the
second under pressure:

- **Deprecation** is planned and advance-notice — something will stop working,
  on a known date, with time to migrate.
- **A breaking change** is a fact about a release that already happened — this
  version behaves differently than the last one, and a consumer needs to know
  before they upgrade, not after something fails.

